  "answer_text": "The latest iPhone lineup includes the **iPhone 17, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone Air, and the newest iPhone 17e**. Here's where you can buy them:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcf1 Current iPhone Lineup\nApple's current flagship iPhone lineup includes the **iPhone 17e** (2026), **iPhone 17**, **iPhone 17 Pro**, **iPhone 17 Pro Max**, and **iPhone Air** (all 2025).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\uded2 Where to Buy\n\n1. **Apple Store (Online & In-Person)**\n   The best place to start is directly from Apple. You can choose two-hour delivery from an Apple Store, free delivery, or easy pickup options. When you buy directly from Apple, you'll get access to Personal Setup \u2014 guided online sessions where a Specialist can walk you through setup and data transfer or help you explore new features.\n   - \ud83c\udf10 [apple.com/iphone](https://www.apple.com/iphone/)\n\n2. **Best Buy**\n   Shop Best Buy for the latest Apple iPhone and accessories, including the newest iPhone models.\n   - \ud83c\udf10 [bestbuy.com](https://www.bestbuy.com/site/mobile-cell-phones/iphone/pcmcat305200050000.c)\n\n3. **T-Mobile**\n   T-Mobile carries the full Apple lineup, including the iPhone 17 Pro Max, iPhone 17 Pro, iPhone 17e, iPhone Air, and iPhone 17.\n   - \ud83c\udf10 [t-mobile.com](https://www.t-mobile.com/cell-phones/brand/apple)\n\n4. **Other Carriers** (Verizon, AT&T, etc.) \u2014 Most major carriers also carry the latest iPhones, often with trade-in deals or installment plans.\n\n5. **Amazon** \u2014 You can find both new and certified refurbished iPhones on Amazon, often at competitive prices.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Trade-In Option\nWhen you're ready to buy a new iPhone, you can trade in your current iPhone or Android device and apply any credit toward your purchase. If your device isn't eligible for credit, Apple will recycle it for free.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Budget Tip\nThe **iPhone 17e** is Apple's most affordable 2026 iPhone. For $599, you get the A19 chip, 256GB of base storage, MagSafe charging, and a 48MP Fusion camera.\n\nWould you like help choosing which iPhone model is right for you?",
